Testing the question-scoped pending model further (follow-up to #2882) — I hit a case where a whole-store `affects()` mark doesn't just pend the store, it **gates tracked data readers out of an optimistic write entirely**. The spec says optimistic writes are verdict-inert and stay visible; here they never render.

## Repro

`solid-js` / `@solidjs/signals` **2.0.0-beta.18**, vite dev:

```tsx
const [users, setUsers] = createOptimisticStore(() => getUsers(id()), []);

const run = action(function* () {
  affects(users);                                   // declared: this data is changing
  setUsers((u) => {
    u.push({ name: "Ryan", email: "dfad@fs.com" }); // optimistic insert
  });
  yield api.save();
  refresh(users);
});

<Loading fallback="Loading...">
  <For each={users}>{(user) => <h2>{user.name}</h2>}</For>
  <button onClick={run}>Run</button>
</Loading>
```

Click Run: **Ryan never appears** — not in the `<For>`— for the whole action. Delete the `affects(users)` line and the row pops in instantly. Moving `affects` after the push doesn't help; the ordering only changes mark *coverage* of the new record (the spec'd snapshot-at-declaration rule), not this.

